[node name="FanLabel" type="Label" parent="Labels"]
offset_left = 160.0
offset_top = 1020.0
offset_right = 700.0
offset_bottom = 1080.0
text = "1. FAN
squishy rides the stream, rocky only sinks more slowly in it.
the ledge is higher than any single launch: ride up,
then shoot again from inside the stream (grounded.launchFromFan)."

[node name="CableLabel" type="Label" parent="Labels"]
offset_left = 700.0
offset_top = 680.0
offset_right = 1260.0
offset_bottom = 740.0
text = "2. CABLE
squishy is thrown by the rope, rocky lands in it dead.
solid from above, pass straight up through it from below."

[node name="TrampolineLabel" type="Label" parent="Labels"]
offset_left = 1380.0
offset_top = 1000.0
offset_right = 1940.0
offset_bottom = 1060.0
text = "3. TRAMPOLINE
rocky is launched, squishy is not.
shoot rocky in at an angle -- the pad keeps 60% of it."

[node name="LeverLabel" type="Label" parent="Labels"]
offset_left = 1700.0
offset_top = 640.0
offset_right = 2240.0
offset_bottom = 700.0
text = "4. LEVER
rocky weighs 6 to squishy's 1, but at the shipped torqueScale
BOTH drive the plank to its stop -- only the SPEED differs.
that saturation is the open question in docs/PORTING.md.
rocky cannot climb here: go up as squishy, switch in mid-air."

